.github/workflows/docker.yml's PR "Test Docker image" step does three things after the --version check:
- starts the built image detached, with the checkout mounted at its own runner path and published on 127.0.0.1;
- fails unless curl to http://127.0.0.1:<port>/health from the runner reports "status": "healthy" and that projectPath;
- removes the container on every exit path.
HEAD's image fails that curl.
